===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|nighte}}, {{m|enm|night}}, {{m|enm|nyght}}, {{m|enm|nicht}}, {{m|enm|niȝt}}, {{m|enm|nacht}}, {{m|enm|naht}}, from {{inh|en|ang|niht}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*naht||night}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*nahts||night}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*nókʷts||night}}.

Cognate with {{cog|sco|nicht}}, {{m|sco|neicht||night}}, {{cog|fy|nacht||night}}, {{cog|nl|nacht||night}}, {{cog|nds|Nacht||night}}, {{cog|de|Nacht||night}}, {{cog|da|nat||night}}, {{cog|sv|-}} and {{cog|no|natt||night}}, {{cog|fo|nátt||night}}, {{cog|is|nótt||night}}, {{cog|got|𐌽𐌰𐌷𐍄𐍃||night}}, {{cog|el|νύχτα||night}}, {{cog|ru|ночь||night}}, {{cog|sa|नक्ति|tr=nákti||night}}, and {{cog|la|nox||night}}, whence English {{doublet|en|nox|notext=1}}, a {{glossary|doublet}}.

